WEBVTT

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:04.480
Then we're at an impasse.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:08.640
If you have a problem with the 
Neutscheland Company's prices,

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:11.370
then you can go elsewhere.

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:12.760
That so?

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.150
We're outta here, Elch.

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:16.240
H-Hey!

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:18.150
And where are we supposed to go?!

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:20.120
Elch.

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:27.130
If you happen to find another buyer
in Dormundt, I hope you'll tell me.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:34.230
We'd have to report anyone doing business 
here without one of these permits.

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:40.970
Hold on!

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:42.680
I told you, didn't I?

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:45.820
That's the only trading company
in this town!

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:47.610
They're the only ones we can sell to!

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.080
No way.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.660
I enjoy fleecing people,

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:55.030
but I hate it when they try to fleece me.

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:57.630
What are you saying?
You're not making any sense!

00:00:57.630 --> 00:00:59.780
Neither are you.

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:04.400
A deal is a means of 
achieving your objective.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:08.010
Any deal that doesn't help you reach your goal
is one that's not worth making.

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:11.960
Could you achieve your goals 
at the prices he was offering?

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:13.200
I mean, yeah...

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:16.920
At those prices, our village
wouldn't make it through the winter.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:19.470
Even I understand that.

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:21.580
But we can't do anything about it!

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.730
A life spent going along with the flow
and letting yourself be used is worthless.

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:30.930
He was so condescending to you.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:33.920
You can't take that lying down.
It's not right.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:38.380
Y-You're... angry on our behalf?

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:39.840
Of course I am.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:42.080
We owe you all our lives.

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:47.690
Hey, Elch, let me take charge
of this business trip.

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:52.710
If you do, I'll earn you a fortune
and teach them a lesson.

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:56.720
And while I'm at it,

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:01.620
I'll also crush this shitty company in a week.

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:26.370
<b>High School Prodigies Have It Easy
Even In Another World!</b>

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:39.490
<b>Masato Is Serious
About Making Money!</b>

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.510
Come on, come all!

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:40.920
What I hold here before you is nothing 
more than an ordinary handkerchief,

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:42.490
a simple piece of cloth.

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:46.280
Yet this cloth is about to undergo 
a miraculous transformation,

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:48.740
so watch closely, everyone.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:50.930
Here we go.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:51.750
There!

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:57.860
Wow!

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:00.010
Incredible!

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:08.170
Go, girl!

00:04:08.170 --> 00:04:09.950
You're amazing, Miss!

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:10.720
Huh?

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:14.060
Um, I'm a boy, you know.

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:14.910
Yeah, yeah.

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:15.770
You're funny.

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:18.730
You've all really been a huge help.

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:21.490
Everyone in the village is 
really happy to have you, too.

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:25.380
No, we're the ones who should be
thanking you for all your help.

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:31.050
We're merely doing what little each of us can

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:34.170
to repay this village for
the kindness it has shown us.

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:46.180
It's our general consensus that 
we'd like to be of use to you all.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:53.610
So I'll work diligently to make 
more mayonnaise again today.

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:56.160
It's not just the mayonnaise.

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:59.260
You've taught us a lot of new recipes,

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:01.910
making it so much more fun to cook!

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:03.380
But that said...

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:08.320
We'll run out of salt and wheat flour soon.

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:10.710
You don't need to worry.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:14.430
The Merchant and Shinobu went with Elch

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:16.900
when he headed into town 
to prepare for the winter.

00:05:17.970 --> 00:05:20.840
I'm sure we'll receive 
the necessary goods soon.

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:27.050
I just hope Elch is getting 
along with those two.

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:33.850
We can't afford... 
to keep seven useless mouths fed!

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:37.430
If your wounds are healed, 
then get out of our village already!

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:43.030
He can be really stubborn.
I wonder who he got it from.

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:45.820
Oh, Winona.

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:51.700
He acts that way toward all of you
because of his position as our treasurer.

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:57.760
He's trying really hard to ensure that
everyone in the village is well-fed,

00:05:57.760 --> 00:06:00.140
but things aren't looking too good.

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:05.260
It's all due to that Jaccoi guy.

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:08.830
Jaccoi? Who is that?

00:06:08.830 --> 00:06:12.510
He's the guy who's monopolized 
the right to trade in Dormundt.

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:17.900
He's an awful fellow taking advantage 
of our small businesses by paying peanuts.

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:19.100
I see.

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:21.100
Though, in that case,

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:24.530
everything will be perfectly okay
if we just let the Merchant handle it.

00:06:25.850 --> 00:06:30.030
That guy is like capitalism
in human clothing,

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:32.550
so a situation like that 
is sure to stoke his fire.

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:38.920
By now, he's probably...

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:43.770
in the process of establishing his own 
Elm Trading Company or something like that.

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:48.580
Business Permit...

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:51.110
Elm Trading Company...

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:55.720
Mayor of Dormundt, Walter Von Haizerad...

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:57.930
Th-This...

00:06:57.930 --> 00:07:01.290
i-isn't fake, is it?

00:07:01.290 --> 00:07:05.650
I think it'd be more challenging to enter 
the mayor's home and leave with a fake.

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:08.650
How did you manage to...

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:13.960
Given my talent for gathering intel,
it was more than easy enough.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:17.950
Ah! You! When did you get here?!

00:07:18.610 --> 00:07:19.880
Nin, nin!

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:22.460
Listen, Elch, give it some thought.

00:07:22.820 --> 00:07:28.460
If Neutscheland is the only one handling 
all the trade in a town as big as Dormundt,

00:07:28.890 --> 00:07:31.580
then there has to be something 
going on behind the scenes.

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:33.470
Huh? You mean...

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:36.090
The Mayor's secret account books

00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:38.970
showed a vast sum of money 
coming from Neutscheland.

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:42.150
So when I questioned him about that a little,

00:07:43.910 --> 00:07:46.470
I got one of these as my answer.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:48.730
Seriously?

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:49.960
Now then...

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:53.630
I'll be taking my leave.

00:07:53.630 --> 00:07:56.160
There's a lot more information 
I need to gather, after all.

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:58.060
Yeah. Thanks, Shinobu.

00:08:00.550 --> 00:08:01.660
On that note...

00:08:02.050 --> 00:08:04.170
Let's go stock up, Elch.

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:06.170
Huh? Stock up?

00:08:06.510 --> 00:08:08.410
But we're here to sell these, right?

00:08:08.410 --> 00:08:09.320
Why would we...?

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:12.380
Ow! What was that for?!

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:14.640
You asked a stupid question.

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:16.870
What do you think we got this permit for?

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:19.630
Listen, this is a good opportunity.

00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:22.970
I do owe your village
for saving us, after all.

00:08:22.970 --> 00:08:23.690
Huh?

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:28.300
The President of the Sanada Group
is gonna give you

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:30.690
a personal lecture on how to make money.

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:34.310
I'll let you feast your eyes on
an armful of coins real soon.

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:37.130
Really?

00:08:39.230 --> 00:08:42.020
An armful of coins?

00:08:42.550 --> 00:08:44.330
I want that, too.

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:45.830
Me, too.

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:48.460
I want gold.

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:52.340
I want to make my own living.

00:08:52.770 --> 00:08:55.720
I've had enough of living under other people.

00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:57.270
So...

00:08:57.680 --> 00:08:59.090
Please.

00:08:59.090 --> 00:09:00.560
Please,

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:03.230
teach Roo how to make money, too!

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:12.720
Very well.

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:14.240
Starting now, you're one of us.

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:16.650
Hey, are you serious?!

00:09:16.650 --> 00:09:20.010
You're letting some random kid join our group?!

00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:21.490
Of course I'm serious.

00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:24.060
There's greed in her eyes.

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:27.660
Adding people like her to 
your ranks can't hurt.

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:30.650
I'm Sanada Masato.

00:09:30.650 --> 00:09:32.170
This is Elch.

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:35.010
And, young lady, your name is Roo?

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:37.440
Yeah, I'm Roo.

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:38.270
All right!

00:09:38.270 --> 00:09:42.640
Okay, Rooko, I'll teach you 
how to make money as well!

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:45.020
Yeah! Thank you, Teacher!

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:46.020
Teacher?

00:09:47.990 --> 00:09:48.900
Whatever.

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:52.270
Listen, we're now the Elm Trading Company.

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:54.010
So keep up with me!

00:09:54.450 --> 00:09:57.580
It's time to have some fun making money!

00:09:57.580 --> 00:09:58.410
Yeah!

00:09:59.230 --> 00:10:01.160
Oh, but before that,

00:10:01.730 --> 00:10:04.150
we'll need to get you looking the part.

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:20.840
Consignment sale?

00:10:21.980 --> 00:10:23.180
What's that?

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:24.570
I've never heard of it.

00:10:24.570 --> 00:10:25.600
Same, same.

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:27.120
Long story short,

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:31.180
the Elm Trading Company will be setting
up shop in the central plaza tomorrow,

00:10:31.180 --> 00:10:34.610
and we'll let Fitze Village
sell your wares alongside ours.

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:37.070
Y-You can do that?!

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:40.000
But we don't have a permit.

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:41.110
Uh-huh.

00:10:41.110 --> 00:10:43.020
We can.

00:10:43.020 --> 00:10:45.800
It's not like it's prohibited.

00:10:45.800 --> 00:10:49.670
Also, our Elm Trading Company has this permit.

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:56.590
However, it did cost us quite 
a bit to obtain this thing.

00:10:57.680 --> 00:11:03.050
So we'd be taking 20 percent of 
your sales as a hosting fee.

00:11:06.690 --> 00:11:07.660
Well...

00:11:08.720 --> 00:11:12.040
We're all in the same boat of 
suffering under Neutscheland.

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:14.750
So if you're willing to help man the shop,

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:18.360
we don't mind making an exception 
and reducing the hosting fee to 10 percent.

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:20.610
How's that?

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:23.900
Hey, how much is 10 percent?

00:11:23.900 --> 00:11:24.780
Hmm...

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:26.440
Hey, I don't know.

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:30.620
Listen, let's say you were selling carpets.

00:11:31.030 --> 00:11:36.380
From what I could see in the market, 
the going rate on those was about 450 luc.

00:11:37.400 --> 00:11:39.500
If you brought them to Neutscheland,

00:11:41.410 --> 00:11:44.630
they'd buy them from you for 150 luc at best.

00:11:46.280 --> 00:11:49.800
Now, let's say you sell them on 
consignment with our trading company.

00:11:49.800 --> 00:11:54.010
We'd be selling them for a little less 
than market price, so about 400 luc.

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:58.090
Once they sold, we'd take 10 percent,
or 40 luc, for ourselves.

00:11:58.790 --> 00:12:03.400
Which means you would be taking home 360 luc.

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:07.660
We'd be earning that much?!

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:09.640
That's incredible!

00:12:09.640 --> 00:12:11.850
Please let us in on this!

00:12:11.850 --> 00:12:15.420
Hey, would it be okay if we mentioned 
this offer to other villages, too?

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:16.630
Yes!

00:12:17.440 --> 00:12:19.660
We'd welcome it, brethren!

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:23.180
We'll be counting on you tomorrow, then.

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:25.100
Yeah, leave it to us!

00:12:28.420 --> 00:12:30.470
Well, that's how you do it.

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:34.810
But is what you just proposed 
really going to work that well?

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:37.310
What? You're worried about it?

00:12:38.020 --> 00:12:41.210
It seems way too convenient for us

00:12:41.210 --> 00:12:44.240
to be able to stock up 
without paying a single luc.

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:45.820
Well, just wait and see.

00:13:02.790 --> 00:13:04.590
Incredible!

00:13:04.960 --> 00:13:07.090
Are you serious?

00:13:12.460 --> 00:13:17.350
We really got stock without 
spending a single luc...

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:19.930
Listen up, you two.

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:22.800
When you're stocking up a business,

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:25.740
you'll naturally need money.

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:29.370
However, the one thing 
you need more than money

00:13:30.150 --> 00:13:31.370
is trust.

00:13:31.370 --> 00:13:33.020
Trust?

00:13:33.020 --> 00:13:40.120
In business, trust breaks down to, 
"How much profit can they make me?"

00:13:40.120 --> 00:13:44.970
In other words, nothing holds more trust 
in this town than a business permit.

00:13:45.380 --> 00:13:49.280
Also, Elch, you've already 
figured it out, haven't you?

00:13:49.280 --> 00:13:51.300
What makes this method especially nasty?

00:13:52.240 --> 00:13:53.790
We're not spending any money,

00:13:53.790 --> 00:13:57.520
so we can stock up all we want, <i>and</i> we
won't lose anything if it doesn't sell.

00:13:57.520 --> 00:14:00.880
We just keep generating profit at no risk.

00:14:00.880 --> 00:14:01.900
Right?

00:14:02.290 --> 00:14:05.600
Unfortunately, you only get a 50 for that.

00:14:05.600 --> 00:14:06.360
Rooko,

00:14:07.190 --> 00:14:11.070
do you remember what I said 
the condition would be

00:14:11.070 --> 00:14:13.520
for reducing their hosting fee
from 20 percent to 10?

00:14:13.520 --> 00:14:16.760
Uh, uh...

00:14:18.400 --> 00:14:20.750
You said they'd have to help man the shop!

00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:24.280
Yes, that's the crucial part.

00:14:28.600 --> 00:14:32.260
Doing that allows our small 
three-person trading company

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:36.980
to expand our shop as much as we need.

00:14:37.570 --> 00:14:41.980
We could become even bigger 
than Neutscheland, in fact.

00:14:54.650 --> 00:14:57.850
We aren't getting any customers. 
Is this really going to work?

00:14:57.850 --> 00:14:59.940
Well, don't panic.

00:15:01.140 --> 00:15:04.130
Oh, my. When did they 
build a market out here?

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:07.050
Oh? This is pretty cheap.

00:15:08.420 --> 00:15:10.220
Welcome, welcome!

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:14.080
We're Elm Trading Company, 
the cheapest option here in Dormundt!

00:15:14.080 --> 00:15:16.490
Our goods are less expensive, 
but the quality's just as good!

00:15:16.490 --> 00:15:17.770
Have a look around!

00:15:18.130 --> 00:15:20.080
Oh! They have a lot of stuff!

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:22.770
There's more than just Neutscheland, huh?

00:15:22.770 --> 00:15:25.340
We're getting lots of customers.

00:15:25.340 --> 00:15:26.660
Naturally.

00:15:27.510 --> 00:15:29.100
I'll take these shoes.

00:15:27.510 --> 00:15:30.990
Our shop is closer to their daily sphere 
and cheaper than their usual shops.

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:30.680
I'll take this cape.

00:15:30.990 --> 00:15:32.030
Now, come on, you guys!

00:15:32.470 --> 00:15:34.240
I'll take everything on this row.

00:15:32.470 --> 00:15:34.520
Sell, sell, sell away!

00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:35.280
M-Me too!

00:15:36.180 --> 00:15:39.580
And that's what I've learned about Jaccoi.

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:42.540
<i>Well, that's about what I anticipated.</i>

00:15:42.900 --> 00:15:44.420
<i>Thanks, Shinobu.</i>

00:15:45.730 --> 00:15:47.340
<i>You're welcome.</i>

00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:48.630
Oh, one more thing.

00:15:49.080 --> 00:15:50.550
Hmm? What is it?

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:52.780
We earned a fair deal today,

00:15:52.780 --> 00:15:56.170
so I'm going to acquire a cart 
full of supplies for the village.

00:15:54.070 --> 00:15:56.720
Coins, coins...

00:15:57.120 --> 00:16:00.730
<i>We should probably fulfill Ringo-chan's 
request sooner than later.</i>

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:02.380
Right.

00:16:02.380 --> 00:16:05.480
Then give me a call
once you've got everything ready.

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:08.860
I'll deliver it for you at express speed.

00:16:14.230 --> 00:16:16.990
Nin, nin, nin!

00:16:24.770 --> 00:16:26.880
Salt and pepper.

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:29.900
Oh, even sugar!

00:16:29.900 --> 00:16:31.210
Honey Jam!

00:16:31.210 --> 00:16:32.630
There's so much!

00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:34.280
Look at this!

00:16:34.280 --> 00:16:36.160
Wow, incredible!

00:16:36.160 --> 00:16:37.850
There's even fruit!

00:16:37.850 --> 00:16:40.520
I stopped by Ringo-chan's place already.

00:16:40.870 --> 00:16:42.170
Good work.

00:16:42.610 --> 00:16:44.920
Now we can stop worrying about the lab.

00:16:45.490 --> 00:16:47.130
How's the Merchant doing?

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:51.080
Everything's going well.

00:16:51.080 --> 00:16:54.120
He should be coming back 
in about three or four more days.

00:16:54.120 --> 00:16:55.000
Oh?

00:16:55.660 --> 00:17:01.580
He did say he would crush the 
Neutscheland Trading Company in a week.

00:17:01.960 --> 00:17:03.240
I see.

00:17:03.240 --> 00:17:07.330
If the Merchant made that proclamation, 
then it'll probably come true.

00:17:08.240 --> 00:17:10.170
Elm Trading Company?!

00:17:10.170 --> 00:17:13.930
I don't need you bringing me information 
about a tiny company like that.

00:17:13.930 --> 00:17:15.790
Just let them do as they please!

00:17:15.790 --> 00:17:17.800
P-Pardon me!

00:17:18.340 --> 00:17:19.770
Good grief!

00:17:19.770 --> 00:17:22.680
What is Count Haizerad even thinking?!

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:26.330
What does he think I'm paying 
him all that money for?!

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:32.540
Those stupid farmers will go bankrupt
in no time, so I can leave them be.

00:17:32.540 --> 00:17:36.360
Raising a fuss over every little 
thing is what small-timers do.

00:17:39.270 --> 00:17:43.210
Those fools will be gone before you know it.

00:18:08.650 --> 00:18:10.520
Give me that! Give me that!

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:11.650
Give me mayo!

00:18:15.060 --> 00:18:16.600
Thank you, come again!

00:18:17.600 --> 00:18:19.690
We finally get a break.

00:18:19.690 --> 00:18:21.120
Don't slack off.

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:24.120
Good grief, the big part is yet to come.

00:18:24.560 --> 00:18:27.100
Rooko, make sure you tidy up, okay?

00:18:25.430 --> 00:18:29.920
Mayo, mayo, mayo.

00:18:32.240 --> 00:18:36.890
Would you sell me a container 
of mayonnaise as well?

00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:39.400
Nice to meet you.

00:18:39.400 --> 00:18:43.560
I am the captain of the
merchant fleet Sea Serpent.

00:18:43.990 --> 00:18:46.060
My name is Klaus.

00:18:46.060 --> 00:18:47.960
I've been waiting.

00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:51.560
I'd love to have you try some of this for us.

00:19:02.150 --> 00:19:03.950
Sea Serpent.

00:19:04.280 --> 00:19:08.960
The grand merchant fleet handling
maritime trade out of Eastern Freyjagard.

00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:11.160
I've heard much about you.

00:19:11.160 --> 00:19:12.710
What a coincidence.

00:19:13.130 --> 00:19:16.120
I happened to hear of a new trading company

00:19:16.120 --> 00:19:19.290
doing some interesting 
business here in Dormundt.

00:19:51.700 --> 00:19:54.970
S-Sea Serpent switched sides?!

00:19:55.680 --> 00:19:59.670
W-Well, fine.

00:20:00.150 --> 00:20:04.180
Starting tomorrow, we'll open a 
market in the central plaza too.

00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:06.650
This is war!

00:20:06.650 --> 00:20:09.640
I'll make them regret making an enemy

00:20:09.640 --> 00:20:12.180
out of the Neutscheland Trading Company!

00:20:21.470 --> 00:20:23.180
Coins.

00:20:23.180 --> 00:20:24.620
So...

00:20:24.620 --> 00:20:26.160
m-many...

00:20:26.500 --> 00:20:28.810
coins!

00:20:32.520 --> 00:20:33.950
What's wrong, Elch?

00:20:33.950 --> 00:20:35.670
Oh, nothing.

00:20:36.040 --> 00:20:38.040
Worried about Neutscheland?

00:20:40.480 --> 00:20:42.730
W-Well, yeah.

00:20:43.810 --> 00:20:45.800
That's an incredible amount of coins!

00:20:46.630 --> 00:20:49.080
Use the damn door.

00:20:49.080 --> 00:20:50.770
Business is thriving, I see!

00:20:54.690 --> 00:20:57.770
Hmm, so this girl is Roo-chan, huh?

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:00.810
Looks like she can't hear me.

00:21:00.810 --> 00:21:04.510
I think she's even more 
fond of money than I am.

00:21:04.510 --> 00:21:08.360
Wow, that suggests a promising future.

00:21:08.740 --> 00:21:12.710
Since you're here, 
I'm guessing they're making their move?

00:21:12.710 --> 00:21:14.000
Bingo!

00:21:14.770 --> 00:21:18.170
They're planning to go to war,
starting tomorrow.

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:20.200
W-War?!

00:21:20.200 --> 00:21:22.680
They're going to start buying up goods

00:21:22.680 --> 00:21:25.000
and selling them with no mind 
for profit on either end.

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:26.980
It's basically a free-for-all.

00:21:30.210 --> 00:21:33.130
They must have confidence 
in going blow for blow.

00:21:33.560 --> 00:21:37.060
It's certainly not a bad play, though.

00:21:37.400 --> 00:21:38.720
No.

00:21:38.720 --> 00:21:39.990
It's not a bad one.

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:43.570
But only if they had gone with it
on our first day.

00:21:54.320 --> 00:21:56.340
Wh-What?!

00:21:56.710 --> 00:21:58.360
Who are they?!

00:21:59.670 --> 00:22:03.500
The blades that will kill off
Neutscheland for me.
